repository-code: "https://github.com/dopalici/neuroscope"
url: "https://github.com/dopalici/neuroscope"
abstract: >-
  NeuroScope is a real-time consumer EEG dashboard for the Interaxon Muse 2
  headband. It acquires four-channel EEG (TP9, AF7, AF8, TP10 at 256 Hz),
  optional PPG, and IMU via Lab Streaming Layer (muselsl / pylsl), then runs
  bandpass filtering, Welch band-power estimation (delta–gamma), contact-quality
  checks, blink/jaw artifact detection, and non-clinical cognitive-state
  heuristics (beta/alpha focus ratio, relative-alpha calm, frontal alpha
  asymmetry). A React frontend provides live visualization and a simple
  alpha-driven neurofeedback demo. Simulation mode supports development without
  hardware. Educational and exploration tooling only — not a medical device.
keywords:
